---
import MainLayout from "../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
---

<MainLayout title="Home">
  <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row items-center gap-8">
    <img
      src="/ejhumphrey.png"
      alt="Eric J. Humphrey"
      class="w-48 h-48 rounded-full object-cover shadow-lg"
    />
    <div>
      <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2">Eric J. Humphrey, PhD</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-600">
        World-Class Technologist with a Founder's Mindset
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section class="mt-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold mb-4">About Me</h2>
    <p class="text-gray-700 py-2">
      I build the teams, technology, and strategy that fuel growth. My career has spanned the spectrum: 
      a researcher at Google alongside AI pioneers, a leader for Spotify's highest-stakes personalization projects, 
      an instructor at MIT, and the founding tech lead for a Sequoia-backed startup.

    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 py-2">
      This unique background lets me operate at any altitude: I can architect a company's AI strategy, 
      rebuild a culture to be inclusive and high-performing, and still ship the code for a product's 
      first iteration. At heart, I’m a founder-first leader who thrives on turning ambitious ideas 
      into tangible revenue, whether that's sparking a viral PLG loop or unlocking a new enterprise market.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 py-2">
      My career began in music, a path that led me to my dream job at Spotify shaping next-generation AI. 
      I then pivoted to ed-tech and health, seeking to apply my skills to more mission-driven work. 
      Today, I believe climate is the defining challenge of our time, and my ambition is to look back on 
      my career and know I made a material contribution to the health of our planet.

      That same energy now pulls me toward climate tech, specifically Direct Air Capture (DAC). 
      I’m undeterred by the skepticism around it; I’ve seen once-fringe ideas like deep learning 
      reshape the world. I see immense potential in using captured CO₂ as a feedstock for new 
      fuels and materials, a vision I’m passionate about sharing with anyone who will listen.
    </p>
    <p class="text-gray-700 py-2">
      I’m an avid runner (my favorite way to explore a new place) and a curious 
      language learner (French, Norsk, Spanish), forever
      fascinated by how words carry human history, and an occasional homebrewer
      (<i>ahem</i> beer scientist). I’m also a one-person rock band (guitar, drums,
      bass, sax, keys in a pinch) with a knack for songwriting and storytelling.
    </p>
  </section>
</MainLayout>
